# Scalar Commons faucet — operator overrides.
# Installed to ~/.config/scalar-commons/faucet.env (0600) by install.sh.
# Anything set here overrides the unit's Environment= lines, because the unit
# reads this file after them. Commented-out lines show the effective default:
# the unit's, where it sets one, otherwise the faucet's in-code default — the
# unit sets only HOST, PORT, RPC_ENDPOINT and TRUST_PROXY.
#
# This file is the one that holds a signing key, which is why install.sh
# creates it 0600 and never overwrites an existing one.

# HTTP bind address. Loopback only: the faucet sits behind the nginx vhost, and
# its rate limits are an application-level defence, not a network one.
#FAUCET_HOST=127.0.0.1
#FAUCET_PORT=8082

#FAUCET_RPC_ENDPOINT=ws://127.0.0.1:9944

# Signing account. REQUIRED before any public exposure.
#
# There is no in-code default: the faucet refuses to boot without this, and
# refuses any //Name dev seed unless FAUCET_ALLOW_DEV_SEED=true. It used to
# fall back to //Ferdie, a PUBLISHED Substrate dev seed whose account
# held ~1e9 CMN, so anyone could have emptied it with a plain balances.transfer
# the moment RPC went public — every rate limit below and the reserve above
# would have protected nothing. docs/history/TESTNETAUDIT.md §6 I-6, issue #123.
#
# Generate one and put the phrase HERE, in this 0600 file, never in the unit:
#   ./target/release/scalar-node key generate --scheme sr25519 --output-type json
#
#FAUCET_SEED=<24-word secret phrase>
#FAUCET_SS58_FORMAT=42

# Per-request drip, and the balance below which the faucet refuses to drip.
# The reserve is what keeps the faucet from draining its own account to the
# existential deposit and dying mid-drip.
#
# Registering an agent costs ~1050.01 CMN (minStake 1000 + baseRegistrationFee
# 50 + ED 0.01 + fees). At 10 CMN a stranger needed 106 drips over ~4.4 days
# (#137, I-21); at 1100 one drip cleared registration by 49.99 CMN, so a single
# 100 CMN demo transfer before registering stranded the tester behind the
# 60-minute per-address window (#162). 1500 leaves ~450 CMN of slack; with the
# per-IP budget unchanged the worst case is 7 500 CMN/hour/IP.
#FAUCET_DRIP_CMN=1500
#FAUCET_RESERVE_CMN=1000

# Rate limits. Per-address stops one agent farming the faucet; per-IP stops one
# host farming it across many addresses.
#FAUCET_ADDRESS_MAX_REQUESTS=1
#FAUCET_ADDRESS_WINDOW_MINUTES=60
#FAUCET_IP_MAX_REQUESTS=5
#FAUCET_IP_WINDOW_MINUTES=60

# Total budget across every requester (F11, #20): the only limit that bounds
# what the faucet itself can lose, however many addresses and IPs ask. At the
# default drip, 50 a day is 75 000 CMN. When either is spent, drips answer
# 503 FAUCET_PAUSED with Retry-After and the journal gets one ALERT line.
#FAUCET_GLOBAL_HOURLY_MAX=20
#FAUCET_GLOBAL_DAILY_MAX=50

# Where the limits are kept so a restart does not reset them. Absolute path
# (Node does not expand ~). Deleting the file is the deliberate reset; a corrupt
# one stops the faucet at startup instead of silently starting empty.
#FAUCET_STATE_FILE=/home/dev/.local/state/scalar-commons/faucet-limits.json

# A drip's three waits: its turn at the balance check, inclusion in a block,
# finality. Together they must stay under the 60 s agents and nginx wait.
#FAUCET_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS=10
#FAUCET_INCLUSION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=18
#FAUCET_FINALITY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=24

# Only true behind a proxy that OVERWRITES X-Forwarded-For.
#
# Both halves of this had to be fixed before it was safe to turn on, and both
# are now in the repo:
#   1. deploy/public/nginx/'s template sets X-Forwarded-For to $remote_addr
#      instead of appending, so a caller cannot contribute an entry at all.
#   2. clientIp() reads the RIGHT-most hop, so even behind an appending proxy
#      the key is the one entry a remote caller cannot choose.
#
# Neither depends on the other being right. With TRUST_PROXY=false behind any
# proxy the per-IP limit is one global bucket for the whole internet, which is
# useless; with it true and an appending proxy read left-most, it was
# forgeable, which is worse. Issue #123.
#FAUCET_TRUST_PROXY=false
